<PageLayout title="Export & Download Grok Conversations — TotalRecalls" description="How to back up and export your xAI Grok conversations into local Markdown and JSON files on Windows using TotalRecalls." breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Guides", href: "/guides/" }, { label: "Grok" }]}>
  <h1>How to Download &amp; Archive Grok Conversations</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    xAI's Grok (<code>grok.com</code>) has evolved rapidly into a primary engine for real-time news analysis, coding,
    and open-ended reasoning. TotalRecalls connects to your active Grok session and converts your complete chat
    history into clean, locally searchable Markdown and JSON file pairs.
  </p>
  
  <h2>Why Grok Requires a Dedicated Archiving Path</h2>
  <p>
    Unlike static coding assistants, Grok conversations heavily incorporate live web citations, real-time X (formerly
    Twitter) post references, and dynamic system reasoning. While xAI offers a manual data dump under <em>Settings &rarr;
    Data Controls</em>, that feature generates an unwieldy, monolithic JSON file delivered by email that cannot be easily
    searched or viewed in everyday document editors.
  </p>
  <p>
    TotalRecalls solves this by extracting each thread individually, naming each file pair by date and topic, and
    formatting embedded X post citations directly as readable blockquotes.
  </p>

  <h2>Step-by-Step Walkthrough</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Launch TotalRecalls:</strong> Select <strong>Grok</strong> from the provider list. (Grok is included
      with Downloader Pro; you can activate your license key at the top of the window).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Connect to Your Session:</strong> Click <em>Connect</em>. A secure embedded Chromium window opens to
      the official Grok sign-in page. Sign in with your X account or email credentials. Your login cookies are
      stored exclusively in the local app cache on your machine and never transmitted anywhere else.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Verify Conversation Count:</strong> Once authenticated, TotalRecalls enumerates your account history
      and displays your total conversation count (e.g., <em>Connected · 84 conversations found</em>).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Select Destination:</strong> By default, files are saved to <code>%USERPROFILE%\TotalRecalls-download\Library\grok\</code>,
      or you can select any custom local directory.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Download:</strong> Click <em>Download my conversations</em>. The application streams your chats to
      disk with live progress indicators. For subsequent runs, use <em>Download latest only</em> for a fast incremental sync.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Output Format Specifics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Preserved X Post Embeds:</strong> When Grok cites a live post or news thread, the Markdown export
      renders the post author, text preview, and direct permalink so you never lose the source context.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Model Version Metadata:</strong> Every exported file includes YAML frontmatter indicating whether the
      turn was generated by Grok 2, Grok 2 mini, or Grok 3.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dual Format:</strong> Each chat yields both a readable <code>.md</code> document and an uncompressed
      <code>.json</code> file ready for vector indexing or scripting.
    </li>
  </ul>
</PageLayout>
